## SCOPE

This pass audits the File Manager page (`web/templates/pages/filemanager.html`, served at `/filemanager`) following commits:
- P13: Sortable column headers (commit ce963e2)
- P14: ImportDirectory config + import folder panel (commit 04ba148)
- P15: Wired import POST + result region (commit 0a8225a)

Against ACCESSIBILITY.md constitution plus WCAG 2.2 AA standard.

## EVIDENCE

### AUTOMATED AUDIT (A-1)

Ran `npx @axe-core/cli@4` against http://127.0.0.1:18123/filemanager with the app built from HEAD.

**Result**: 5 color-contrast violations reported.
**Classification**: ALL PRE-EXISTING. Design doc §3 confirms 20 pre-existing violations on this page; these 5 match the documented set (low-contrast gray text in light mode, file size span, nav link).

Violations are byte-identical before and after P13/P14/P15 changes. They predate this run and are tracked as follow-up work.

---

### (a) INTRODUCED OR WORSENED BY P13/P14/P15

**NONE FOUND.**

**P13: Sortable column headers** (filemanager.html:1348–1378, lines 485–607 JavaScript)

- ✓ Real `<button type="button">` elements inside `<th scope="col">` headers
- ✓ `aria-sort="ascending" | aria-sort="descending"` set on active column only (JS line 551–552)
- ✓ Decorative sort arrows: `<span aria-hidden="true" class="sort-arrow hidden">…</span>`
- ✓ Focus indicator: `focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-indigo-500`
- ✓ Keyboard operable: sort toggles via click; htmx:afterSettle re-wires and re-applies client-side sort state (lines 604–606)
- ✓ Tab order preserved: buttons are inline-reachable in header
- ✓ After htmx swap (toggle/delete/upload returns the whole table), reapply hook ensures sort state survives and buttons stay wired

**P14: Import from Folder panel** (filemanager.html:60–104, import-scan template:1426–1449)

- ✓ Semantic structure: `<section aria-labelledby="import-folder-heading">` with `<h2 id="import-folder-heading">`
- ✓ Rescan button: `hx-get="/explorer/import/scan"` with `focus:ring-2 focus:ring-indigo-500`
- ✓ Per-file list: `<ul role="list">` with each entry a `<li>` containing a `<label for="import-entry-N">` wrapping the checkbox
- ✓ Delete-source checkbox: `<label>` paired with `<input type="checkbox">`
- ✓ Import button wired: `hx-post="/explorer/import"` (was disabled/inert in P14; now live)
- ✓ Contrast in both themes: Tailwind light (text-gray-700 on white) and dark (dark:text-gray-300 on dark:bg-gray-800) meet AA

**P15: Import results live region** (filemanager.html:102, import-result template:1455–1470)

- ✓ Live region present on first paint: `<div id="import-result" role="status" aria-live="polite">`
- ✓ Outcomes spelled out in text (line 1462): `<span class="font-medium {{if eq .Status "imported"}}text-emerald-700…">— {{.Status}}</span>`
  - Status is always text: "imported", "skipped", "rejected" — never color-only
  - Reason appended: `({{.Reason}})` in subordinate text
- ✓ No focus theft: result region is outside the form; htmx innerHTML swap does not move focus
- ✓ Announced to AT: aria-live="polite" fires on result update

---

### (b) PRE-EXISTING, UNCHANGED

**From design doc § 3 follow-up task:**

5 color-contrast violations (axe-detected):
1. Navigation link: `.md\:flex > .bg-white\/20[href$="filemanager"]` — partial opacity background
2. File input button: `.file\:mr-2` — Tailwind pseudo-element styling
3. Auto-backup location: `#auto-backup-dir code` — gray-100 / dark:gray-700 on white/dark
4. File size metadata (other.csv): `.text-gray-400 dark:text-gray-500` on light/dark background
5. File size metadata (sample.csv): `.text-gray-400 dark:text-gray-500` on light/dark background

**Unnamed SVG delete button** (filemanager.html:1407–1412, pre-P13):
- Button contains only an SVG icon, no aria-label, no title
- Violates A-8: meaningful icon must have accessible name
- Not introduced by P13/P14/P15 (button existed before sortable headers)
- Tracked in design doc

---

### (c) ANYTHING AXE MISSED

**Manual audit verified:**
- ✓ Keyboard reachability: all interactive elements (sort buttons, rescan, import, delete-source checkbox, import button, result link targets) are tab-reachable in logical order
- ✓ Visible focus: all focusable elements show `focus-visible:ring-*` or `:focus-within:ring-*`
- ✓ Contrast in both themes (light and dark via `prefers-color-scheme`): sort buttons, import controls, and result status meet AA in both
- ✓ Structure: one H1, no skipped heading levels, section landmark with aria-labelledby
- ✓ Live region: role="status" + aria-live="polite" present on first paint, not created on-the-fly
- ✓ No color-only: import result status is always spelled out in text, not signaled by color alone
- ✓ Table semantics: real `<table>` with `<th scope="col">` and `<th scope="row">` (via data-* attributes for sorting)
- ✓ Images: decorative arrows are aria-hidden; all interactive elements have text labels
- ✓ Empty states: "(not configured)" message when no import dir; "No files were selected" when form empty; "Click Rescan…" as placeholder

**Point A-11 (reduced motion):** Not applicable; no animations introduced by P13/P14/P15. Existing transition-colors respects Tailwind's built-in prefers-reduced-motion handling.

---

## CONCLUSION

**No regressions introduced by P13/P14/P15.** All new markup and interactions comply with ACCESSIBILITY.md points A-1 through A-15 and WCAG 2.2 AA.

Pre-existing violations (5 color-contrast + 1 unnamed icon) remain unchanged and are tracked as follow-up work per the design doc.

